ed task notes. Came up when plan-derived task had null description and needed standalone context for automation.\n\n  01KJGA18 (1 day ago by Jacob Chapel) [bug, infra, skills, setup]\n    Diagnose skill verify drift/no-hash for plugin-provided core skills.\n\nObserved behavior:\n- kspec skill verify reports codex statuses as drifted/no-hash for help, observations, triage, reflect, triage-inbox, writing-specs.\n- kspec skill diff reports plugin-provided (no local render to diff).\n- Rendered skill files exist under .agents/skills.\n\nInvestigate:\n- render-hash semantics in .kspec/skills for plugin-provided skills\n- plugin-provided status handling in skill verify/status/diff paths\n- whether this is expected behavior or a bug in drift detection\n\n  01KJG5A7 (1 day ago by Jacob Chapel) [bug, ralph, codex, sessions]\n    Task budget false-positive outside ralph loop when stale KSPEC_SESSION_ID is present (observed in codex session). Repro: with KSPEC_SESSION_ID set to an old session that has budget.json started_this_cycle=max_per_cycle, 'kspec task start @ref' fails with 'Task budget exhausted ... let iteration end naturally' even when not running ralph and no in-progress tasks. Expected: budget guard should apply only during active ralph loop iteration context, or stale/non-ralph session IDs should be ignored.\n\n  01KJF69V (2 days ago by @claude) [cli, validation]\n    kspec validate should warn about items with identical titles in the same module — two items both named 'Generation Progress UX' with different ULIDs caused confusion during a fix session in imgen project\n\n  01KJDZBA (2 days ago by @claude) [testing, ralph, infra]\n    Add second mock adapter registration for ralph tests. Currently --adapter-cmd registers a single 'custom' adapter, making it impossible to test different adapter IDs in real (non-dry-run) runs. Options: (1) --worker-adapter-cmd / --reviewer-adapter-cmd flags, (2) env-based adapter registration (e.g. KSPEC_TEST_ADAPTERS JSON), (3) allo